{
  "correction_rules": [
    "Persistent low bias: model forecasts are generally below realized prices by ~+1 to +3 EUR for horizons ~D+1 to D+20. Apply an upward level shift, larger in the first 2–3 weeks.",
    "Trend/impulse underreaction: after an upswing starts, the model lags and fails to carry the rally far enough (misses the 68–70 zone). Add positive momentum correction when the last 5–10 days show rising prices.",
    "Late-horizon crash overshoot: at longer horizons (~D+20 to D+30) the model often predicts an exaggerated sell-off (e.g., dropping into low 60s) that does not materialize. Damp negative moves beyond ~2 EUR/day and pull forecasts back toward the recent 10–15d mean.",
    "Mean-reversion timing error: the model reverts too early and too strongly after strength; delay mean reversion when spot is above its 10–20d average and realized volatility is elevated.",
    "Volatility compression: forecast path is too smooth versus outcomes during rallies; widen forecast bands and allow higher peaks when recent realized vol is increasing."
  ]
}
